<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Kinematics: finding constants from velocity information (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A particle moves so that its position after \( t \) seconds is</p>
\[ s(t) = p\,t^2 + q\,t \quad \text{metres}, \]
<p>where \( p \) and \( q \) are constants. At \( t = {@t1@} \) s the velocity is \( {@V1@} \) m/s, and at \( t = {@t2@} \) s the velocity is \( {@V2@} \) m/s.</p>
<p>(a) Write down \( v(t) \) in terms of \( p \), \( q \) and \( t \).</p>
<div>\( v(t) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Form two equations and solve them to find \( p \) and \( q \).</p>
<div>\( p = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<div>\( q = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(c) Find the acceleration of the particle.</p>
<div>\( a = \) [[input:ans4]] m/s\(^2\) [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> \( v(t) = s'(t) = 2pt + q \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Use the two velocity facts (not position facts):</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
v({@t1@}) &= {@2*t1@}p + q = {@V1@} \\
v({@t2@}) &= {@2*t2@}p + q = {@V2@}
\end{align*}
\]
<p>Subtract the first equation from the second: \( {@2*(t2 - t1)@}p = {@V2 - V1@} \), so \( p = {@pv@} \). Then \( q = {@V1@} - {@2*t1@}({@pv@}) = {@qv@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( a(t) = v'(t) = 2p = {@2*pv@} \) m/s\(^2\). This is constant: the velocity changes by the same amount every second.</p>
<p>So \( s(t) = {@pv*t^2 + qv*t@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
